{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-24T05:04:17.314Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.2-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e318d53a2002017270f9daae","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.2-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-24T05:04:17.314Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"The newer harness rejects undeclared arrays before dispatch. Mark selectors and usage flags repeatable; keep scalar phase fields refused as extension_flag_value_invalid and preserve parser-level INVALID_REQUEST. The import helper now checks for an existing ID under its lock, so fixture setup removes a disposable document before importing and tests the precise overwrite refusal. With only the old flag declarations restored, the harness rejected repeated IDs and the installed CLI kept one of two citations. Reverting the changelog flag fails its regression. All three checks pass with the fixes. Clean-home strict health, typecheck, build and the docstring gate pass. Changelog generation kept all 3 published dependency bullets and restores 53 historical bullets."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-24T05:04:17.314Z"}],"before_hash":"9c764ed2d063cd28792c6e605390aac8f78c4a8a1e8842512a15d00b86c8d023","after_hash":"c4193abdb58a681feed66fc7f13f98181d08517e2d47bc3de18aaea8762379a1","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"88181c11159e626df36376ee2043fe24b4ebf535029fbc4e564